# API Documentation Rules

- Whenever adding or modifying API integrations, always update related documentation.
- Documentation must include:
  - API purpose
  - Endpoint URLs
  - Authentication method
  - Request parameters
  - Response examples
  - Rate limits
  - Error handling
- Documentation files should be placed under `/docs`.
- Never leave API integrations undocumented.
- If an API behavior changes, update the existing documentation in the same commit.
